  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-47066" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Continue CAPMiR Implementation and Coordination for Joint Support with UNHCR and UNICEF</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the project is to address the persistent humanitarian and protection needs of the targeted population groups at key transit migration locations across the country. This will be done through strengthening the existing CAPMiRs (Tecun Uman and Quetzaltenango) and through the establishment of additional CAPMiRs in other key locations, based on preliminary context and needs assessments as well as in coordination with PRM. Through the implementation of a sustainable approach, IOM will work in collaboration with its local partners in order to focus its interventions on reducing the protection risks of migrants and other population groups in vulnerable situations thereby contributing to addressing irregular migration at large.</narrative>
  </description>
